.SH NAME
tmpfile \- create a temporary file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B
.SM FILE
.B "\(**tmpfile (\|)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tmpfile\^
creates a temporary file and returns a
corresponding
.B
.SM FILE
pointer.
Arrangements are made so that the file will
automatically be deleted when the process using
it terminates.
The file is opened for update.
.SH FILES
/usr/tmp	directory for temporary files
.SH SEE ALSO
creat(2),
unlink(2),
fopen(3),
mktemp(3),
tmpnam(3).
